    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe consolidation is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Logic in the right unit.** `getIdentityKey()` is a derived, `@Transient` property on the `Owner` entity, sitting naturally alongside the existing derived getters (`getCityRegion()`, preferred-contact-channel). This is the right home: it serves double duty as the API-exposed `readOnly` field (openapi.yml) and the dedup key, with no duplicated key-construction logic in the controller \u2014 the controller just compares.\n\n- **No orphaned code.** I verified `toE164` is still used by `normalizeTelephone` (line 345), so it did not become dead when `rejectDuplicateTelephone` was removed. `findHouseholdMembers` now has exactly one remaining caller (`assignHousehold`), which the updated javadoc accurately reflects.\n\n- **Exception layer collapses cleanly.** The three duplicate exceptions correctly become one (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`, sensibly reusing the former email exception file), and `ExceptionControllerAdvice` loses two handlers plus two now-unused message constants \u2014 a genuinely additive simplification, not a catch-all. The single handler mirrors the shape of the ones it replaced.\n\n- **Controller create-flow reads well.** The per-field reject calls are replaced by one `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner)` invoked after telephone/email/household are set, so the method operates on a fully-populated owner \u2014 a coherent ordering a maintainer would find natural. The javadoc documents the normalization precondition clearly.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
